2026-10-18: Populate decoded guest data/stack memory-access metadata for base
and CB instructions (BIT [HL] reads only; modifying CB operations read/write;
conditional stack operations describe their possible access).
Reference: https://github.com/gbdev/pandocs/blob/master/src/CPU_Instruction_Set.md
The fields were previously always zero. Keep memory accesses alone from proving
a branch-target prefix; require the decoded store/DEC/JR NZ loop when setup
extends beyond the original prefix window. Remove the previously dead load-only
rejection: copy/fill routines are valid code. The first broad metadata candidate
exposed an overly permissive prefix check and was rejected before integration.
Validation: all 512 opcode access classifications; RST target with a long store
initializer; wrong loop back edge rejected; real Super Mario Land 1 strict boot.
